# scripts/e2e.d/GO-ONLY — product files no E2E bundle proves, each with the Go test(s) that do:
#   <glob> <TestName>[ <TestName>…]
# scripts/select.sh selects NO bundle for a change to one of these (the Go pass of T0/T1 is its proof).
# The E2E self-test refuses a row whose glob matches no product file and a test name that does not exist.
# Two tokens stand in for a test where a file is never run on this box, and say so instead of naming a
# test that does not touch it:
#   @cross-compile  built only for windows/amd64 — scripts/check.sh's Go stage compiles it; no test runs it
#   @not-built      built for no target this project ships (the `!unix && !windows` fallback); vet sees
#                   nothing of it either — the line is here so the coverage rule does not hide the fact
internal/store/fake.go TestFakePutGetStatListDelete TestFakeFailNext TestFakeConcurrentSafe
cmd/clippet/freebytes_windows.go @cross-compile
internal/worker/freebytes_windows.go @cross-compile
internal/store/fs_sync_windows.go @cross-compile
cmd/clippet/datalock_windows.go @cross-compile
cmd/clippet/freebytes_other.go @not-built
internal/worker/freebytes_other.go @not-built
